  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Nosophora parvipunctalis Hampson 1896 (2022) in Zenodo. 41 download(s) recorded.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Nosophora parvipunctalis Hampson 1896 (2022) in Zenodo is authored by Singh, Navneet, Ranjan, Rahul and Talukdar, Avishek. Topics: Table (database), Ancient history, History, Geography and South asia.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">No citations yet.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "ArticleStory",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This scholarly article has a modest but visible early usage record: 83 views and 41 downloads in Zenodo, alongside an open-access repository presence and linked biodiversity data resources. It has not yet accrued citations in OpenAlex, and there is no recorded scite or public-discourse activity in the available record.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The article presents a focused taxonomic record for <em>Nosophora parvipunctalis</em> Hampson, 1896, summarizing type locality and distribution information and situating the species within both historical and regional records. Its scholarly footprint is still early-stage, but the repository metrics show that the work has been accessed and downloaded, indicating practical interest in the specimen and distribution information it consolidates.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of reach comes from Zenodo usage data, which records 83 views and 41 downloads. The work is openly available through a repository with DOI-based persistence, and it is connected to a companion data object, suggesting that the article is part of a broader stewardship package rather than a standalone text. Related identifiers also link the record to biodiversity infrastructure, including GBIF and other domain repositories, which supports re-use in taxonomic and biodiversity workflows.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the citation record is currently quiet: OpenAlex reports 0 citations, and scite lists no citing, supporting, or contradicting papers. That pattern does not imply lack of value; rather, it indicates that any later scholarly uptake has not yet appeared in the indexed citation layer available here. The public-discourse record is similarly sparse, with no captured event-data mentions.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, this is a well-stewarded open-access scholarly item whose immediate signal is usage and infrastructural integration rather than citation impact. For a taxonomic work, that combination often matters: the article is discoverable, citable, and linked to downstream biodiversity resources, even though its formal citation footprint has not yet developed in the available record.</p>",
